## Why This Is Asked

Tests a fresh DP angle: interval-based value depends on distinct characters within each substring, plus precise reconstruction for k blocks.

## Key Concepts

- Non-overlapping interval DP
- Precomputing distinct counts for all substrings
- Reconstruction via back-pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
function maxKSubstrings(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dist = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const freq = new Array(26).fill(0);
    let setBits = 0;
    for (let j = i; j >= 0; j--) {
      const idx = s.charCodeAt(j) - 97;
      if (freq[idx]++ === 0) setBits++;
      dist[j][i] = setBits;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  const start = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][0] = 0;
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      // Option 1: skip i
      if (dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
        prev[i][t] = i-1;
        start[i][t] = start[i-1][t];
      }

      // Option 2: end t-th substring at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const val = dp[s-1][t-1] + dist[s-1][i-1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = s-1;
          start[i][t] = s-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct substrings
  const result = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (prev[i][t] === i-1) {
      i--;
    } else {
      result.unshift([start[i][t]+1, i]);
      i = prev[i][t];
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][k], substrings: result };
}
```

Time complexity: O(n²k) for DP transitions + O(n²) for preprocessing. Space: O(n² + nk). Optimizations include limiting the inner loop or using convex hull tricks for special cases.

## Why This Is Asked
This tests a practical DP pattern: partitioning a string into k+1 substrings with a sum objective and exact k cuts, including reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with exact cuts
- Substring value computation via prefix powers of 10
- Backtracking to recover split points

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumPartition(s, k){
  const n = s.length;
  const a = s.split('').map(Number);
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  const pow10 = new Array(n+1).fill(1);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){pref[i] = pref[i-1]*10 + a[i-1]; pow10[i] = pow10[i-1]*10;}
  const val = (l,r)=> pref[r]-pref[l-1]*pow10[r-l+1];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){ dp[i][0] = val(1,i); }
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      for(let j=0;j<i;j++){
        if(dp[j][t-1]===-Infinity) continue;
        const cur = dp[j][t-1] + val(j+1,i);
        if(cur>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=cur; pre[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct using n and k
  let cuts=[]; let i=n, t=k; while(t>0){ const j=pre[i][t]; cuts.push(j); i=j; t--; }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], cuts};
}
```

